<title>USA: High Plains Wheat--Dealers take 3-5 cts protection.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat--Dealers take 3-5 cts protection.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain merchandisers in the U.S. High Plains said Monday they were taking widespread three to five cents per bushel protection on hard red winter wheat.</p>
<p>The protection came as grain and oilseed futures were expected to open sharply lower after beneficial rains fell Saturday over dry soy- and corn-growing regions of Illinois.</p>
<p>CBOT's Project A overnight trend for wheat was four to five cents lower.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, basis levels for HRW wheat were unchanged, and dealers said movement was slow.  </p>
